Changes:36 states under {{$NEXT}} that "New error codes -32020 (HeaderMismatch), -32021 (MissingRequiredClientCapability) and -32022 (UnsupportedProtocolVersion) are wired into _jsonrpc_error". Verified: -32021 appears nowhere in lib/ or t/ - zero hits. -32020 and -32022 do exist.

handle() checks io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities for key presence only (exists, not shape or contents), so there is no per-capability requirement that could raise -32021.

Two possible resolutions, needs a call:
a) The feature was intended but never landed - implement a required-capability check that raises -32021, per MCP 2026-07-28.
b) It was dropped deliberately - then the Changes line must be corrected before release, because it goes out as release notes claiming an error code consumers can handle.

The two matching README claims were already corrected in 23708ff. Changes was left untouched on purpose: rewriting a changelog entry is a maintainer call, not a doc cleanup.
